AB  - With the increasing complexity of institutional workflows and information management, there is a growing need for intelligent platforms that can adapt to dynamic data requirements and ensure secure, scalable interactions. In our work, we have used FastAPI for high-performance backend services, replacing Flask to accommodate asynchronous operations and robust API handling. FastAPI leverages LangChain for orchestration of advanced chains and agent-based workflows, enabling Robotic Process Automation (RPA) in response generation using prioritized AI-Based hybrid semantic data retrieval System. A conditional logic pipeline has been implemented wherein the token size of retrieved context determines the processing route: if the token count is below a defined threshold, lightweight LLMs such as Llama 3 accessed via externally hosted APIs through a unified LLM wrapper are used for inference. For larger token contexts, data is first distilled through older models like GPT-2 or BART before being passed to newer LLMs, thus improving both efficiency and answer quality. Additionally, tools such as LangSmith have been integrated to streamline debugging, evaluation, and prompt optimization. Furthermore, the memory module within LangChain is leveraged to enable reinforcement learning-based adaptation and iterative performance improvements.Evaluations show the hybrid LLM pipeline achieved a BLEU score of 91.2, ROUGE score of 88.4, and precision of 90.1, with user upvote rates reaching 96% and fallback rates as low as 2%. The adoption of FastAPI contributed to significantly reduced response times under concurrent user loads. The LangSmith-integrated feedback loop accelerated prompt refinement and error reduction across sessions. This work contributes to the field by demonstrating a generalized framework for intelligent academic automation, integrating conditional LLM routing, explainable evaluation, and modular RPA pipelines for institutional applications.
