AB  - The rapid development of large language models (LLMs) has shown great potential in code generation and attracted much attention in the industrial automation community. This paper investigates and evaluates the capabilities of contemporary LLMs, including ChatGPT, DeepSeek, Perplexity, Gemini, and Mistral, in generating programmable logic controller (PLC) codes for discrete manufacturing processes. The automatic generation of PLC code in the IEC 61131-3 compliant languages, instruction list (IL) and structured text (ST), is tested using three case studies of different complexity. The findings indicate that while each LLM possesses distinct strengths in generating PLC code, ChatGPT currently emerges as the most adaptable for this purpose. Both the direct and indirect PLC code generation by LLMs are considered. The effect of single-shot prompting and iterative prompting is also analyzed.
