AB  - LLM-assisted RTL generation often suffers from syntactic and logical errors, requiring manual verification. For the first time, we propose a shift from direct code generation to formal specification. Using Conjunctive Normal Form (CNF) as compact, verifiable representation of circuit functionality, we introduce an LLM-based synthesis framework, RTL-Forge, which generates CNF specifications and deterministically compiles them into Verilog. We explore two approaches; first, finetuning a lightweight open-source LLM on RTL-CNF pairs to quickly generate verifiable CNF and correct RTL for small-/midsized circuits; second, leveraging SoTA reasoning models with incremental prompting to scale to large designs while avoiding hallucinations. The first approach outperforms tools like Verigen and RTLCoder, while the second scales to larger circuits.
ER  - 

